"notes": ["Source: Bills 2026 media guide, 'ALL-TIME REGULAR SEASON' record pages 225-242 (passing 228-230, rushing 231-233, receiving 234-235, interceptions 237, sacks 238). Everything is regular season; postseason, opponent, team and rookie lists were skipped.","through_season 2025: the tables include 2025 seasons (e.g. James Cook III 2025 Buf 1621 rushing yards, Josh Allen 2018-2025, Jordan Poyer 2017-2025).","Every transcribed row was read from 200 dpi crops of the page pictures; the leaders tables were also checked arithmetically (yards per attempt/reception/return equals the printed Avg column) and against the IA OCR text.","Game lists: the guide prints dates with 2-digit years (9/15/02). 'years' holds the same date with a 4-digit year (60-99 -> 19xx, 00-26 -> 20xx; the guide's records start in 1960); 'raw' keeps the printed text including opponent.","complete_to = number of player rows the guide prints for that list (tied rows count separately); 'rows' may hold fewer when only the top 10 (career tables) or top 5 (season table) were transcribed.","Tied groups in the box lists print the rank and value once and then stack several players under it; each of those players is a row with the shared rank, tie true, and a raw like '(2.) 5 Name date' (parenthesised rank = inherited).","Guide numbering quirks (kept as printed): game passing yards prints rank 2 for both the 424 and the 419 row (values differ, tie false); season passing yards and season rushing yards skip or repeat rank numbers below rank 5 (not transcribed beyond rank 5).","career pass_td has both a 'list' (the 3-row MOST TD PASSES, CAREER box) and a 'column' (the TD column of the 20-row passers table by yards) so ranks 4 and 5 (Fitzpatrick 80, Kemp 77) can be recovered; use the list for ranks 1-3.","career rec is the ALL-TIME LEADING RECEIVERS table (descending by Rec). career rec_yds and rec_td are the top-5 boxes on the same page.","career rush_td includes quarterback rushing TDs (Josh Allen 79) as printed. Sacks are since 1982 only, per the guide's own note.","Names are as printed: 'James Cook III' in tables/career boxes but 'James Cook' in the season rushing TD box; the guide's season receptions box prints 'Stefon Digg' for the 2022 row (kept evident Diggs in name, typo noted on the row).","Cross-check inside the guide: page 259 ('BILLS BEST PERFORMANCES') repeats the single-game top values (273 rushing yards O.J. Simpson 11/25/76, 5 rushing TDs Gilchrist 12/8/63, 463 passing yards Bledsoe 9/15/02, 6 TD passes Kelly 9/8/91, 15 receptions Reed 11/20/94, 265 receiving yards Evans 11/19/06, 4 receiving TDs Beebe and Butler) and agrees with the lists here.","Tackles: the guide has no tackles record list for any scope."]
}
